meta {
  name: admin-truck-force-delete
}

docs {
  # VAHN_ADMIN force-delete of trucks (plutus-java PR #1141, branch topic/admin-truck-force-delete)

  Covers `DELETE /api/trucks/admin/{id}` (204, no body) and `DELETE /api/trucks/admin/list`
  (200, `[{truckId, success, errorMessage}]`), both VAHN_ADMIN only. They soft-delete a truck even
  when it is VERIFIED, unassigning its driver first. The existing `DELETE /api/trucks/{id}` and
  `/api/trucks/list` still refuse VERIFIED trucks (steps 7-8 are the contrast check).

  Run requests 1-15 in order on staging. Pass the VAHN_ADMIN token at run time so it is never stored:

      npx @usebruno/cli run bruno/flows/plutus-api/admin-truck-force-delete --env staging \
        --env-var plutusApiTruckForceDeleteAdminToken=<VAHN_ADMIN token>

  The static VAHN_ADMIN token (plutus-java config.yml, auth.static_tokens.role_tokens) works on
  staging, or log in as a real VAHN_ADMIN. Step 1 logs in the torg admin `plutusApiTruckForceDeleteTorgPhone` as the
  non-admin caller for step 9.

  Test data: it creates three throwaway trucks (A verified, B verified, C unverified) in torg
  `plutusApiTruckForceDeleteTorgId` and deletes all three. It never touches an existing truck.
  Verification uses `mark-as-verified`, which needs a primary PAN card on that torg.
  Not covered: the driver-unassign part (no driver is attached). All captured values are runtime
  vars (`bru.setVar`), so nothing is written to the environment file.
}
